WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.740
<v 0>The one important note, especially if you're trying to save on tokens,</v>

2
00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.640
is that since these routines do run on a regular schedule,

3
00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.580
you may need to be a bit more mindful around the model that you're

4
00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:12.180
using for these scheduled tasks. Let's say you set up a routine like this

5
00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.760
where it's just a daily reminder of things to keep in mind.

6
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.060
What I would do in this case is just edit this routine,

7
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.400
and from here you can change the model from the default,

8
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.720
which is usually opus, which is the most expensive one,

9
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.020
at the moment, into something like haiku, which is the cheapest model that I'm

10
00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.120
tropic has. So if you click save on that,

11
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.460
that will actually go a long way, as you build up more routines in

12
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:33.600
order to save your tokens and so that you don't hit your usage limits

13
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.240
very early.
